# Phase 0 Implementation Report — v2.5.0 baseline reconciliation

Date: 2026-10-24
Application version remains: 2.5.0 (Phase 0 changes are test/diagnostic/packaging corrections, not a functional OCR release).

## Changes implemented

### 1. Fixed the failing panel integration test

File: `tests/full-system.test.js`

The prior test accessed `StringSelectMenuBuilder.data.options`, but with real discord.js 14.27.0 the option list is present in the serialized payload produced by `.toJSON()`. The production panel builder was valid; the test was coupled to an internal builder representation.

The test now serializes the buttons and select menu with `.toJSON()`, checks the custom IDs, checks all event values, and additionally checks the labels. This is an assertion/API-contract correction; the user-visible bot logic was not changed.

### 2. Added report output-path control

File: `scripts/run-reported-screenshot-regression.js`

The runner accepts `REPORTED_SCREENSHOT_REPORT_PATH`. This lets fallback/native runs write into a unique report file without overwriting the tracked historical baseline. The new override was used successfully for the fresh Tesseract.js baseline run.

### 3. Preserved the Phase 0 evidence

